    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured owner-created event in `OwnerAuditor` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/OwnerAuditor.java`), the class the spec designates as the single home for the owner-create audit concern.\n\n**What changed:**\n- After the existing human-readable audit line, `ownerCreated(...)` now also emits an immutable structured JSON event on the same dedicated `AUDIT` logger:\n  ```json\n  {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n  ```\n- **`seq`** is backed by an `AtomicLong` field on this singleton `@Component`, so it increments monotonically across every create for the application's lifetime.\n- **The primary identifier** is read through a small `primaryIdentifier(owner)` seam that returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. Per the spec's forward-looking requirement, when the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, only that one method changes and the event automatically carries the memberId \u2014 no other code needs threading.\n- The JSON is serialized with the project's Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson`) `ObjectMapper`, matching the existing convention in `BindingErrorsResponse`.\n\n**Verification:** The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures). The new `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` confirms an `AUDIT` event line contains the `OWNER_CREATED` marker, the owner id, and the customerCode \u2014 visible in the logs as the emitted event line.",
